  "title": "AlloyDB Read Pools Get Autoscaling!",
  "summary": "AlloyDB now supports autoscaling for read pool instances, allowing you to dynamically adjust resources based on CPU utilization or predefined schedules. This significantly enhances the elasticity and cost-efficiency of your AlloyDB deployments.",
  "details": "A major new capability has been added to AlloyDB: autoscaling for read pool instances. The `ReadPoolConfig` schema now includes an `autoScalingConfig` property, which references a new `AutoScalingConfig` schema. This configuration allows you to define a `Policy` for the autoscaler, including `cpuUtilization` targets (e.g., `utilizationTarget`), `maxNodeCount`, and a `coolDownPeriodSec`. Additionally, you can set up `schedules` using the new `Schedule` schema, enabling time-based scaling with `cronExpression`, `minNodeCount`, and `durationSec`. This feature provides granular control over read replica scaling, optimizing performance and cost.",
